[00:00.57]1. Life, like a mist, appears for just a day,
[00:07.39]Then disappears tomorrow.
[00:14.30]All that we are can quickly fade away,
[00:20.70]Replaced with tears and sorrow.
[00:27.76]If a man should die, can he live again?
[00:34.81]Hear the promise God has made:
[00:37.85](Chorus)
[00:40.89]He will call; The dead will answer.
[00:47.61]They will live at his command.
[00:54.52]For he will have a longing
[01:01.44]For the work of his own hand.
[01:02.18]So have faith, and do not wonder,
[01:02.92]For our God can make us stand.
[01:03.67]And we will live forever,
[01:04.41]As the work of his own hand.
[01:23.90]2. Friends of our God, though they may pass away,
[01:43.39]Will never be forsaken.
[01:50.30]All those asleep who in God’s mem’ry stay,
[01:56.10]From death he will awaken.
[02:04.03]Then we’ll come to see all that life can be:
[02:10.03]Paradise eternally.
[02:26.47](Chorus)
[02:42.91]He will call; The dead will answer.
[02:49.91]They will live at his command.
[02:56.91]For he will have a longing
[03:02.75]For the work of his own hand.
[03:08.59]So have faith, and do not wonder,
[03:20.59]For our God can make us stand.
[03:27.09]And we will live forever,
[03:35.32]As the work of his own hand.